# checkable_binding_witness.rish -- a page claims the checkable room; what binds the claim?
#
# WHY. `context/TWO_ROOMS.md` seats one crossing: "A claim crosses from the vision room to the
# checkable room by exactly one door -- it earns a witness." `tools/t/two_rooms_doorway.rish` reads
# whether a page NAMES a room and stops there, by design, so a settled page declaring the checkable
# room while naming no evidence at all reads exactly like a page bound by six witnesses. This is the
# second half of that promise: the doorway asks whether the door is labelled, and this asks whether
# the label is earned.
#
# WHAT IS GATED, as a ratchet under a ceiling that only falls: `settled_unbound` -- a page whose
# door names the checkable room beside a settled lifecycle word, and whose body names no instrument,
# no tracked module source, and no tracked construction pin. Read 8 on the seating lap over 1,351
# roster pages, of which 435 declare checkable and 202 are settled. A wall at zero would red every
# ship at once over pages nobody chose to touch this hour; the ceiling falls in the commit that
# repairs one.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED, never gated. `settled_delegated` and `settled_hop_dry`: a page saying its
# binding is named on another page -- `foundations/20260905-154954_the-clock-and-the-mark.md`
# writes exactly that, "both halves are law, each bound by a witness the pages below name" -- is
# honest, and the hop is followed ONE step. A delegation that lands is correct as written, so only
# a DRY hop is a promise broken, and that reads 7. One step and no further, deliberately: two needs
# a cycle guard and measures something no reader does.
#
# `roster_absent` is reported for a reason the pen found in this scan rather than the other way
# round: `git ls-files` answers from the index, and one returned path the disk lacks made `awk`
# abort the whole run, so every page after it went unread and the reading printed a clean zero.
# That is the narrowed-glob shape -- the failure that stays quiet. It is counted now.
#
# PROVEN: `tools/fixtures/c/checkable_binding_control.sh`, 40 behaviors on real git repositories in
# a throwaway pen, every refusal planted and then lifted, three mutations asserted to bite, and the
# control's own leg tally asserted beside its verdict.

say "checkable_binding: a checkable door, and what stands behind it"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/checkable_binding_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "checkable_binding: the control must complete"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "checkable_binding: a control leg failed"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "checkable_binding: the control tallied a failing leg"

let reading = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/checkable_binding_scan.sh"]
say reading.out
assert reading.ok else "checkable_binding: the scan must run"
assert reading.out contains "verdict=read" else "checkable_binding: the scan must read the tree before it is believed"
assert reading.out contains "ceiling_ok=yes" else "checkable_binding: settled_unbound stands above its ceiling -- run sh tools/fixtures/c/checkable_binding_scan.sh list"

say "checkable_binding GREEN"
